{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2","id":1186999,"title":"How to balance encounters for Mage E2","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-17T04:08:57-08:00","id":1186999,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How to balance encounters for Mage E2","content":"I am having difficulty wrapping my head around creating encounters in Mage.<br /> <br /> It seems to me, that once mages hit the 4th dot in any arcanum, they are able to stop any encounter in a blink of an eye. It all comes down to who acts first. I will give you a few examples in what I have in mind.<br /> ---<br /> A mage with Fate 4 spell Chaos Mastery (page 138) is able to reduce a subjects next dice pool to a chance die. Because this spells potency is Duration, a single cast, could make the next 3 (you can increase the potency of a spell to Max arcana used - 1) have a chance of a chance die. With a reach you could make a spell of Advanced scale and target up to 10 people with only a 2 die penalty. After the spell is cast all it's left is to either run away or take a bat and play whack a mole and recast the spell every 3rd round. All of this with having a paradox at a chance die.<br /> <br /> A mage with Death 4 spell Enervation (page 132) is able to impose an Immobilised tilt. With 2 reach he could impose an Immobilised tilt up to 10 people with potency of 3, And if using a tool or a yantra he could increase the potency up to 6 and still have a paradox at a chance die for the duration of the scene.<br /> <br /> A mage with Mind 4 spell Hallucination (page 163) can create an illusion that would incapacitate his foes (wall them off, create a firestorm, etc...). <br /> ---<br /> These are just a few examples, to show what I mean.<br /> <br /> Mages are powerful, and I want my players to feel powerful, but I also want to give their foes a fighting chance. My question is what guidelines do you use when creating encounters for your players ? Also perhaps there is a book or a section in the core book that I have missed on this topic.<br /> <br /> I want to emphasise that I do not want to punish my players for thinking of creating ways of using their spells. I just don't want my encounters to be a race condition, where the first mage to cast something gets the cake.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T05:38:25-08:00","id":1187016,"title":"","content":"High Withstands, protective measures which provoke a Clash of Wills, esoteric foes with immunities which have to be figured out (can't Enervate a temporal parasite, or can you?), or foes which hide in strange realities and have to be locked down or fought on their home grounds.<br /> <br /> A larger issue is figuring out what role combat plays in your story.<br /> <br /> I've personally found Mage a very poor game for enjoying combat for its own sake.<br /> When one party member at character creation takes Aetheric Winds and can blast a small gang of humans into unconsciousness with a single spell you really have to reconsider what focus your game has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T05:53:15-08:00","id":1187022,"title":"","content":"You don\u2019t get in fights in Mage unless you want to risk not getting to go first.<br /> <br /> Give opponents decent Withstand, or layered protection, or make the repercussions of conflict ugly so it has to be handled carefully. Make opponents other Mages, from the Lower Depths, the Abyss, or really bizarre.<br /> <br /> You can use simple misdirection as well, stuff where if they get prepared and do their research they can definitely win in a round, but where if they don\u2019t they might be at a disadvantage. <br /> <br /> For instance, once a month people on a certain corner are being Possessed, walked to a particular grave in a cemetery and then cutting their wrists. Which is how the guy -in- the grave died. Seems like ghost possessions on the surface, and if they charge in on just that information geared up with protections vs ghosts they get a surprise. More investigation would have revealed its not a ghost, but a suicide Spirit, it\u2019s experimenting with using its victims and the grave to create a suicide Essence locus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T09:46:30-08:00","id":1187060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1187022#post1187022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don\u2019t get in fights in Mage unless you want to risk not getting to go first.<br /> <br /> Give opponents decent Withstand, or layered protection, or make the repercussions of conflict ugly so it has to be handled carefully. Make opponents other Mages, from the Lower Depths, the Abyss, or really bizarre.<br /> <br /> You can use simple misdirection as well, stuff where if they get prepared and do their research they can definitely win in a round, but where if they don\u2019t they might be at a disadvantage.<br /> <br /> For instance, once a month people on a certain corner are being Possessed, walked to a particular grave in a cemetery and then cutting their wrists. Which is how the guy -in- the grave died. Seems like ghost possessions on the surface, and if they charge in on just that information geared up with protections vs ghosts they get a surprise. More investigation would have revealed its not a ghost, but a suicide Spirit, it\u2019s experimenting with using its victims and the grave to create a suicide Essence locus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Summary: Pride and Hubris are the true Bane of Mages. <hr /><br /> <u><b>Tips:</b></u><br /> Size 6 means Mages have to spend a Spell Factor to increase Scale. Minor, but a few mooks with the Giant merit means they might escape group spells simply by being too big.<br /> <br /> Sleeper crowds risk Paradox and aggravate its effects. It takes a callous manipulator to throw clueless people at a Mage and have their souls scarred by magic, but Mage has no shortage of callous foes available.<br /> <br /> Abyssal entities not only are custom-designed to be Mage antagonists, they draw power from Paradox, compounding other dangers.<br /> <br /> Spell Control limits are A Thing. Throw enough hazzards at a Mage until they start Reaching just to cast. Sure, they can defeat any one of the threats easily - but can they handle <i>eleven</i> at once? Eventually they will run out of Mana to mitigate Paradox... and then the fun begins.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> said, try throwing something unexpected at them. Play upon their assumptions, so that they are <i>mis</i>prepared for a threat. Sure, a Cabal can deal with nearly any foe, but if they spent their efforts preparing for the wrong kind, they are out those resources, and operating under bad tactics.<br /> <br /> Wards and Signs is Prime 2 that grants Withstand equal to its Potency (Duration is the Primary Factor). If a Mage opponent cast upon a group of disposable minions, that is going to make any magic cast upon them harder. Minions get eliminated? Use the freed Spell Control to enchant the next wave and send them in. Attrition is a villain's greatest tool. Remember also that multiple Withstand values add +1 per to the highest value. Even a Potency 1 Wards and Signs with make a Withstand 2 [for average Resolve, Composure, or Stamina] into a 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-17-2018, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T16:49:34-08:00","id":1187164,"title":"","content":"I remember reading something about a Counterspell Numen in Dark Eras. Maybe load up non-human antagonists with that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T18:40:21-08:00","id":1187196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1187164#post1187164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading something about a Counterspell Numen in Dark Eras. Maybe load up non-human antagonists with that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Another Numina/Dread Power might be something like:<br /> <br /> <b>Spell Resistance</b><br /> By spending 1 point of Willpower, you can increase your Withstand rating by 2 for the entire Scene, instead of a single roll.<br /> <br /> Feel free to adjust the effect by making it last only turns, or apply once per Resistance Attribute. Basically it extends the &quot;spend Willpower to boost Withstand&quot; effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T07:07:22-08:00","id":1187280,"title":"","content":"Except Withstand is kind of useless due to the built-in workaround.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T08:59:37-08:00","id":1187295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1187280#post1187280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Withstand is kind of useless due to the built-in workaround.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, first off, getting an ES isn't guaranteed. Second, the ST can always rule that for a particular situation bypassing Withstand is off the table of options for an ES.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T09:48:14-08:00","id":1187304,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you can houserule the problems away, that's what I do, but ES are not that difficult to come by in Mage, that with Praxes only requiring 3 successes to qualify for it and magic aiding by granting Conditions or dice-tricks that help achieving them in the first place. Saying that is not a problem because the Storyteller can just overrule it and make exceptions is technically true but ignores the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T11:07:02-08:00","id":1187318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1187022#post1187022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don\u2019t get in fights in Mage unless you want to risk not getting to go first.<br /> <br /> Give opponents decent Withstand, or layered protection, or make the repercussions of conflict ugly so it has to be handled carefully. Make opponents other Mages, from the Lower Depths, the Abyss, or really bizarre.<br /> <br /> You can use simple misdirection as well, stuff where if they get prepared and do their research they can definitely win in a round, but where if they don\u2019t they might be at a disadvantage.<br /> <br /> For instance, once a month people on a certain corner are being Possessed, walked to a particular grave in a cemetery and then cutting their wrists. Which is how the guy -in- the grave died. Seems like ghost possessions on the surface, and if they charge in on just that information geared up with protections vs ghosts they get a surprise. More investigation would have revealed its not a ghost, but a suicide Spirit, it\u2019s experimenting with using its victims and the grave to create a suicide Essence locus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> These are amazing advices Mrmdubois, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T11:15:38-08:00","id":1187321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1187060#post1187060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Summary: Pride and Hubris are the true Bane of Mages. <hr /><br /> <u><b>Tips:</b></u><br /> Size 6 means Mages have to spend a Spell Factor to increase Scale. Minor, but a few mooks with the Giant merit means they might escape group spells simply by being too big.<br /> <br /> Sleeper crowds risk Paradox and aggravate its effects. It takes a callous manipulator to throw clueless people at a Mage and have their souls scarred by magic, but Mage has no shortage of callous foes available.<br /> <br /> Abyssal entities not only are custom-designed to be Mage antagonists, they draw power from Paradox, compounding other dangers.<br /> <br /> Spell Control limits are A Thing. Throw enough hazzards at a Mage until they start Reaching just to cast. Sure, they can defeat any one of the threats easily - but can they handle <i>eleven</i> at once? Eventually they will run out of Mana to mitigate Paradox... and then the fun begins.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> said, try throwing something unexpected at them. Play upon their assumptions, so that they are <i>mis</i>prepared for a threat. Sure, a Cabal can deal with nearly any foe, but if they spent their efforts preparing for the wrong kind, they are out those resources, and operating under bad tactics.<br /> <br /> Wards and Signs is Prime 2 that grants Withstand equal to its Potency (Duration is the Primary Factor). If a Mage opponent cast upon a group of disposable minions, that is going to make any magic cast upon them harder. Minions get eliminated? Use the freed Spell Control to enchant the next wave and send them in. Attrition is a villain's greatest tool. Remember also that multiple Withstand values add +1 per to the highest value. Even a Potency 1 Wards and Signs with make a Withstand 2 [for average Resolve, Composure, or Stamina] into a 3.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It seems I have somehow forgotten, that sleepers by default do increase a chance for Paradoxes dramatically.<br /> <br /> It's also a valid point that a mage is powerful as long as he has resources. Once he rans out, he's as good as me or you. It's up to the mage to decided how he spends his resources and if he is ok with spending that mana on mortals, I hope he has a good back up plan for bigger fishes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T12:55:52-08:00","id":1187338,"title":"","content":"The max potency for spells isn't arcana -1, you get arcana -1 as the base for primary potency but you can increase it up to whatever. The max is your total dice pool + 5 / 2 up to the -5 limit of a casting dicepool. <br /> <br /> With things like exceptional lucks 9 again turning a chance die into a single die and also giving yourself steadfast via EL too,you can auto succeed at it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-18-2018, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T16:06:10-08:00","id":1187374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1187338#post1187338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The max potency for spells isn't arcana -1, you get arcana -1 as the base for primary potency but you can increase it up to whatever. The max is your total dice pool + 5 / 2 up to the -5 limit of a casting dicepool.<br /> <br /> With things like exceptional lucks 9 again turning a chance die into a single die and also giving yourself steadfast via EL too,you can auto succeed at it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is when you throw Supernal Fae and Abyssals of corrupted Fate/Luck at players who abuse such tricks. Let players achieve what they earn, of course, but if some tactics are starting to ruin the fun, just add a few complications to make things <i>interesting</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T16:28:22-08:00","id":1187379,"title":"","content":"If you don't mind some homebrew, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=997894#post997894\">Grounded</a> (and its Advanced version) might offer some help against Withstand issues. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=953939#post953939\">Spell Thief</a> can also add a few surprises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T17:43:37-08:00","id":1187404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1187304#post1187304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you can houserule the problems away, that's what I do, but ES are not that difficult to come by in Mage, that with Praxes only requiring 3 successes to qualify for it and <b>magic aiding by granting Conditions or dice-tricks that help achieving them in the first place.</b> Saying that is not a problem because the Storyteller can just overrule it and make exceptions is technically true but ignores the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since this is by no means an uncontroversial reading of the mechanics, I feel it necessary to reiterate that there is evidence to suggest that the most flexible applicators of success-altering Conditions don't actually boost spellcasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T22:48:41-08:00","id":1187464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1187404#post1187404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since this is by no means an uncontroversial reading of the mechanics, I feel it necessary to reiterate that there is evidence to suggest that the most flexible applicators of success-altering Conditions don't actually boost spellcasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering Exceptional Luck is the only spell that specifically has the +2 reach for &quot;the boon/hex can affect spell casting rolls&quot; then its safe to assume ALL three applications of boons can be applied vs a spellcasting roll when using EL. Other spells that give boons without this specific +2 reach option (ie monkeys paw, sworn oath etc) can still all all 3 applications of boons to a roll, but can only add the &quot;grant 9/8 again&quot; boon option to spellcasting because THAT specific application of boons has its own +2 reach option that this boon option can apply to spellcasting rolls. The other 2 boon options such as granting bonus dice or giving conditions cant be used on spellcasting rolls when using &quot;monkeys paw&quot;.<br /> <br /> But this is off topic.<br /> <br /> I quickly came to the realization that the best way to balance encounters in mage was to balance the repercussions after whatever encounter. Usually once the PC's had planned for abit the actual &quot;encounter/conflict&quot; was over quickly and i then had to really think about how whatever the PC's had done affected everything around them. Eventually the PC's stopped wondering IF they could do something but considered SHOULD they do it.<br /> <br /> Not had much experience with 2e though, the ES bypassing withstand does indeed make a master with unmaking Life for example a serious threat/encounter to a group of PC's but only if that master has reason to antagonistic to the PC's. Its no wonder masters should be treated with some respect and perhaps people spend time considering if their current action will piss any of them off or not. I like to think most sane Mages dont automatically jump straight to ES unmaking problems away though but my PC's always seem to end up being the insane types who try to violence away problems..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T03:37:57-08:00","id":1187506,"title":"","content":"Live by the Unmaking, die by the Unmaking. There are always more potential enemies. Once they go nuclear, again (as you said) hammer home the consequences of such actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T05:26:00-08:00","id":1187521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1187464#post1187464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering Exceptional Luck is the only spell that specifically has the +2 reach for &quot;the boon/hex can affect spell casting rolls&quot; then its safe to assume ALL three applications of boons can be applied vs a spellcasting roll when using EL. </div> </div> </div> </div>Super debatable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1187464#post1187464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this is off topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> In my experience, the kind of conflict you seem to be looking for, OP, is the kind that only rival mages that are every bit as capable as the PCs can provide. That said, I don't really think Mage is the best game to make that kind of direct conflict a focus anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T08:19:28-08:00","id":1187559,"title":"","content":"I agree with those who say the game should focus mostly on investigation and discovery, rather than direct conflict.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, when it happens I agree that the best ways to make it challenging are:<br /> <br /> - Sleeper witnesses<br /> - Strange immunities and abilities from Temple Guardians, Abyssals, Spirits, Cryptids etc...<br /> - Other Mages with high initiative (many ways to do this like Body Control, Acceleration etc...) and Wards and Signs<br /> <br /> Just remember there's a reason that people talk about the Cold War between Seers and Pentacle Mages: It really can result in a nuclear style exchange with devastating results if people don't respect the &quot;rules&quot; of the game, so to speak.<br /> <br /> What I've done in the early going in my Chronicles is put players up against Sleeper gangs, The Shinje (Boston Unveiled), the Red Word (BU) or low to mid-rank Spirits, Ghosts, Goetia etc... Most of my players get a good idea of the deadliness of the game by that point and usually don't go looking for unnecessary conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T13:13:50-08:00","id":1187627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1187506#post1187506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Live by the Unmaking, die by the Unmaking. There are always more potential enemies. Once they go nuclear, again (as you said) hammer home the consequences of such actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only are there other potential enemies but allies might start retracting any assistance they provide or stop helping out at all if you become known as the one who skips straight to unmaking things away. Who really wants to be friends with people who at the next disagreement might try to end your existence. Once people get reputations for violent thugs its normal that people start distancing themselves from them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T21:07:54-08:00","id":1188072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1187321#post1187321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems I have somehow forgotten, that sleepers by default do increase a chance for Paradoxes dramatically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also found this useful to bear in mind when trying to prevent PCs from turning characters who are intended as recurring villains into paste during the first face-to-face encounter, which is a perennial problem in my group. Finding excuses for such meetings to take place in public places with hundreds of Sleeper witnesses nearby helped tamp down that impulse to go nuclear - both because it puts innocent people in the crossfire and because it makes Paradox much more dangerous. Like the Seer who insisted on parlaying with them at major league baseball games - ones not so packed that it was impossible to get out of earshot of any Sleepers who might overhear talk about the Mysteries, but definitely well-attended enough to ensure that thousands of Sleepers would be witnesses to any spells either party threw around. Further working to the Seer's advantage, the cabal's job in the Consilium was to ensure that local mages didn't get too &quot;noisy&quot; around Sleepers.<br /> <br /> Once the seal on the can of whoopass is broken, combat with mages tends to be short-lived, as others have noted, with the better-prepared combatant or the first one to act enjoying a considerable advantage. It's usually better to focus on the consequences of that violence. A mage who is fighting for her life is more likely to Reach into the stratosphere to preserve it, after all, and I tend to assume that every mage has friends (whether mundane, Awakened, or Something Else) who are likely to come looking for the rival sorcerers who killed their buddy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T05:03:06-08:00","id":1188133,"title":"","content":"Currently running a high exp (15 at the onset, hitting 20-23 exp after 6 months worth of weekly sessions.) <br /> I think 4 out of 5 players have hit 4 dots in one arcana or the other... And I admit, it is a struggle to balance things.<br /> <br /> We are currently playing a heavily homebrewed setting (World war 2 Paris... Seers backing the occupation have wiped out most pentacle mages... Good fun!)<br /> <br /> Thing is from my experience, they can beat up virtually any foe I throw after them... But here is what Ive done to some effect: <br /> <br /> Let them be badass in the individual situation... Sure, if they can get the drop on the enemy, they usually win with comparatively little effort. <br /> But make it dangerous as all hell to do something that &quot;Causes a scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> In my chase, there is an Ochema stalking the players, trying to anticipate the players next move, with the purpose of waiting for them at the would be scene of the crime. <br /> <br /> Now I know that if the players ever go toe to toe with this baddie, they are doomed... And the players know this... So its not a question of wherever they can win the battle of tonights session.. But rather if its worth picking said fight, leaving their nimbus on the scene. <br /> <br /> Dont know if it any way helps... But yeah, make it about the consequences of their actions.. I'm thinking a strong presence of Guardians of the Veil, running an inqusition against anyone breaking the Lex magica? <br /> <br /> Anyway.. Its a bit tangential, but hope it can serve as inspiration:<br /> <br /> TL;DR: I have no idea how to actually balance the individual encounter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Decent storyteller. Poor Banjo player.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12373-sarner","name":"Sarner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12373_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T06:10:29-08:00","id":1188156,"title":"","content":"I think it's important to always keep in mind this fact: World of Darkness is not World of Warcraft.<br /> That's not saying anything bad about WoD or WoW; what I'm saying is that this game isn't primarily geared towards combat as the engine - battles are not the driving force behind what makes this game interesting, fun, or compelling.<br /> Mages start off, innately, the weakest of all the templates: barely more than human, they have no access to the incredible raw power of gauru shapeshifting or the intrinsic resilience of undead flesh and vitae. But Mages seek understanding as a path to power. A Master mage flips the paradigm on it's head: where once the werewolf and vampire had the advantage, they scaled rather linearly, and the mage exponentially. The Master throws around ranged agg damage, and/or has insta-kill spells, and a myriad of utility to support his power. The &quot;payoff&quot; comes late, as mages are slow bloomers. But the payoff is there.<br /> The continued growth beyond Master is a perfect illustration of this point: Archmages exist, whereas no equivalent for Werewolf or Vampire exists. This fully fits the theme of mage the awakening. Werewolf and vampire do not have such themes as transcendence and transcendental power; they grow strong, but stay the same. Improvement is not the same as metamorphosis. <br /> <br /> Which brings up the ultimate point I'm trying to make: balance is not found in crossover. Mage isn't &quot;balanced&quot; against Vampire or Werewolf. The Arcana are only &quot;balanced&quot; against each other in a vague, guideline sense of the word. What is balance in World of Darkness? It's found in story: in consequence, in player satisfaction, in the effect of hubris, vanity, and becoming a human who is not humane. Mage combat is more all-or-nothing than any other template, which is to say either your spells work or they don't, and it's often more efficient to use a gun than a bolt of lightning. Mage isn't built around the combat system. Vampire and Werewolf are more combat-oriented, and engaging/rewarding, if you're looking for combat. Mages either win or lose, often very quickly.<br /> <br /> Don't try to balance Vampires and Werewolves and Mages. It will never happen without homogenizing and nerfing and stripping away most of what makes each character unique. Instead, make sure each player has a niche that they enjoy and effectively fulfill, create an engaging story, and use each splat's built-in challenges to the fullest (when necessary): Mages often require time, time, time to prepare; knowledge of the situation; mana; normal human sleepers interfere with casting; paradox; reach for the best effects; a risk of wisdom loss for the most abusive spells (by abusive I generally refer to the spells people like to complain about).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23924,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","user":"Realmlord","date":". 02-21-2018, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T08:22:45-07:00","id":1209638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1187060#post1187060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wards and Signs is Prime 2 that grants Withstand equal to its Potency (Duration is the Primary Factor). If a Mage opponent cast upon a group of disposable minions, that is going to make any magic cast upon them harder. Minions get eliminated? Use the freed Spell Control to enchant the next wave and send them in. Attrition is a villain's greatest tool. Remember also that multiple Withstand values add +1 per to the highest value. Even a Potency 1 Wards and Signs with make a Withstand 2 [for average Resolve, Composure, or Stamina] into a 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to p114 this isn't true. A spell applies it's Potency to subject's individual withstand ratings. The +1 comes from the attainments. (ie if you're casting through Sympathetic range use whichever withstand <i>rating</i> is higher, which would be either their resistance attribute(s) or the sympathy itself +1.)<br /> <br /> The group I play with are staunch believers that a character isn't a <i>person</i> unless you start with double or triple experience, which makes balancing notoriously difficult and you run into things like &quot;It's Fae/God Machine/whatever therefore any relevant traits are <i>infinite</i>&quot; Which has it's own pros and cons. That being said, we recently fought a D&amp;D inspired mob that was basically a master of Time and clashing with it (even with 4 dots of time myself) was utterly futile. The &quot;Big Stick&quot; approach to balancing may be inelegant but it can certainly work once in a while to just make something absurd with absurd stats (17 defense, lol) forcing the party to work together against a common enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 04-21-2018, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T08:42:02-07:00","id":1209649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1209638#post1209638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to p114 this isn't true. A spell applies it's Potency to subject's individual withstand ratings. The +1 comes from the attainments. (ie if you're casting through Sympathetic range use whichever withstand <i>rating</i> is higher, which would be either their resistance attribute(s) or the sympathy itself +1.)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If a spell has multiple Withstand ratings [\u2026] it uses the highest rating, +1 for every additional rating.&quot;<br /> &quot;When the subject is the target of a spell, that spell is Withstood by the Potency of Wards and Signs.&quot;<br /> The &quot;a spell applies its Potency to individual Withstand ratings&quot; rule means that if you target a group of subjects, the spell checks each individual character's Withstand to see if it affects them individually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T09:04:08-07:00","id":1209652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1209649#post1209649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;If a spell has multiple Withstand ratings [\u2026] it uses the highest rating, +1 for every additional rating.&quot;<br /> &quot;When the subject is the target of a spell, that spell is Withstood by the Potency of Wards and Signs.&quot;<br /> The &quot;a spell applies its Potency to individual Withstand ratings&quot; rule means that if you target a group of subjects, the spell checks each individual character's Withstand to see if it affects them individually.</div> </div> </div> </div>So we're in agreement. If I cast an area spell to say.. Bruise Flesh at potency 5, anyone in the room of stamina 4 or less is affected since it's checked <i>individually</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T09:36:02-07:00","id":1209663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1209652#post1209652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we're in agreement.</div> </div> </div> </div>You contested Vent's statement that casting Wards and Signs on a group of characters at even Potency 1 would grant all of those characters an extra point of Withstand due to their having two Withstand ratings for hostile magic to contend with. That's\u2026 kind of the opposite of agreement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T09:39:44-07:00","id":1209666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1209652#post1209652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So we're in agreement. If I cast an area spell to say.. Bruise Flesh at potency 5, anyone in the room of stamina 4 or less is affected since it's checked <i>individually</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well no, but only cause Bruise Flesh (and all the other direct damage spells) is not normally withstood at all. If your victims had something like a Potency 4 Wards and Signs though, then they would each individually take 1 bashing damage, as their Prime granted withstand reduces your spells potency. <br /> <br /> Spending a WP to boost a Withstand by 2 is also a thing that shouldnt be forgotten. Its often the difference between victory and defeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T10:09:31-07:00","id":1209680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1209663#post1209663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You contested Vent's statement that casting Wards and Signs on a group of characters at even Potency 1 would grant all of those characters an extra point of Withstand due to their having two Withstand ratings for hostile magic to contend with. That's\u2026 kind of the opposite of agreement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I misunderstood. If you target multiple subjects, the withstand rating isn't +1 for each subject after the first is what I was specifically arguing against. Having multiple withstand ratings (ie the like of Wards and Signs and their normal attribute) would certainly provide a +1 as I understand it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T13:03:18-07:00","id":1209750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1209680#post1209680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I misunderstood. If you target multiple subjects, the withstand rating isn't +1 for each subject after the first is what I was specifically arguing against. Having multiple withstand ratings (ie the like of Wards and Signs and their normal attribute) would certainly provide a +1 as I understand it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify, that is what I was saying/suggesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T19:01:12-07:00","id":1209855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1187060#post1187060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Tips:</b></u><br /> Size 6 means Mages have to spend a Spell Factor to increase Scale. Minor, but a few mooks with the Giant merit means they might escape group spells simply by being too big.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I've picked up that Merit on my character. Does that mean that under RAW, I should boost the Scale factor for any spell he casts on himself?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23771-acediamond","name":"aceDiamond","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23771_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T19:03:22-07:00","id":1209857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aceDiamond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1186999-how-to-balance-encounters-for-mage-e2?p=1209855#post1209855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, I've picked up that Merit on my character. Does that mean that under RAW, I should boost the Scale factor for any spell he casts on himself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It is very much a double-edged sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}